7. Preserve functionality and design

This is a copy-editing and presentation-consistency update, not a gameplay redesign.

Do not modify:

* Combat mechanics or movement behavior
* Joystick and classic control functionality
* Combat assist behavior
* Settings persistence or saved-value compatibility
* Keyboard, mouse, touch, or gamepad navigation
* Selection states or focus management
* Modal behavior
* The game’s overall UI layout and visual identity

Do not rename internal settings IDs, localization keys, or control identifiers to match the new display text.

Keep the interface responsive on desktop, tablets, and phones in landscape orientation.

Ensure the corrected text fits comfortably in existing interface elements without clipping, overflow, or awkward wrapping.

