The existing interface tests contain exact string assertions that will need updating.

In particular, review:

* tests/interface/settings.test.mjs
* tests/interface/i18n.test.mjs
* Any relevant CSS or touch-layout editor tests

Update expected strings when the intended display copy changes.

Add focused regression coverage verifying that:

1. Settings headings use sentence case.
2. Classic buttons, Mobile controls, and Combat assist appear correctly.
3. CSS no longer forces Settings headings or badges into uppercase.
4. Both English and French remain correctly localized.
5. Dynamic layout descriptions are grammatically correct.
6. All settings continue to save, load, and respond to player input correctly.

Run the full test suite:

node --test

Do not delete or weaken existing tests merely to make them pass.

9. Final quality review

After implementing the changes, inspect the complete Settings experience in both languages.

Check every category, selectable option, description, badge, and touch-editor control.

Compare the final UI against these requirements:

* No unintended uppercase headings.
* No inconsistent title-case labels.
* No spelling or obvious grammar errors.
* No awkward dynamically generated sentences.
* No broken translations.
* No visual regressions.
* No changes to gameplay functionality.

The desired result is a polished, consistent Settings interface that feels professionally written while retaining Alva’s existing design.

